WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:05.730
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and the BBC just
announced Peter Capaldi’s newest companion

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.759
on Doctor Who, Samuel Anderson.

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:10.570
So I wanted to do a video explaining who he
is and what kind of dynamic he’s going to

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.919
add to the core group of The Doctor and Clara.

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:16.289
I’ll also be doing a follow up Q&amp;A video
later this week so make sure to let me know

00:00:16.289 --> 00:00:17.289
if you want me to include your question in
it.

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:19.551
If you’re finding me for the first time
I usually do bonus videos for really important

00:00:19.551 --> 00:00:20.551
things.

00:00:20.551 --> 00:00:21.551
Like new companions.

00:00:21.551 --> 00:00:22.551
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:00:22.551 --> 00:00:24.249
So let’s do a quick breakdown of Samuel
Anderson.

00:00:24.249 --> 00:00:28.169
His character’s name is Danny Pink and he’ll
also be a teacher at Coal Hill School with

00:00:28.169 --> 00:00:29.169
Clara.

00:00:29.169 --> 00:00:32.610
He’s most known for previously co-starring
with Jenna Louise Coleman on Emmerdale as

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.660
Ross Kirk.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.250
She played Jasmine Thomas.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.860
And for his role on Gavin and Stacey as Fingers.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.970
He co-starred with a few other fellow Doctor
Who Alumni on that show, James Corden who

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.280
played Craig in The Lodger and Closing Time
and Joanna Page who played Queen Elizabeth

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.320
in the 50th Anniversary Special.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.261
Because Radio Times is calling him a new companion
we can assume that at some point he’ll join

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:54.660
Clara and The Doctor in the TARDIS.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.370
During William Hartnell’s run the same thing
happened to teachers Barbara Wright and Ian

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.370
Chesterton.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.260
In that scenario they were really following
The Doctor’s granddaughter Susan Foreman.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.500
So now let’s talk about how he might fit
into the group.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.220
I’m sure everyone is rushing to Netflix
to watch Season 1 all over again to see what

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:11.110
Wright and Chesterton’s run looked like.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.250
All joking aside I think that Moffat is trying
to pay homage to Season 1 with the dynamic

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.800
and maybe even the tone a little.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.580
Peter Capaldi isn’t going to be playing
a version of William Hartnell, it will be

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:24.670
his own original take on the character but
we as whovians will see the similarities.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:29.670
A stern older Doctor with a young eager companion,
joined by a curious scholar.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.940
Practically in terms of Anderson actually
boarding the TARDIS is think it will be something

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:38.331
like Series 5 where Rory was part of the story
for the entire year, but wasn’t in all of

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.530
the episodes.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.240
Especially the first half of the series.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:46.820
Does this mean that by Series 9 Anderson will
board the TARDIS full time like Rory did?

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:51.080
It’s too hard to say as we don’t know
how long Jenna Louise Coleman will stay.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.320
And if she leaves, we don’t know if Anderson
will take over as full-time solo companion.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.520
I really hope that they both stay on for series
9 because it took me almost all of series

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.190
5 just to get used to Arthur Darvill’s Rory.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:05.460
Mostly because he was the butt of so many
of Amy and The Doctor’s jokes until he changed

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.060
into the Centurion Character.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.690
Let’s hope that Anderson doesn’t run afoul
of the Daleks.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:14.579
But the Doctor’s track record with companions
is a little spotty, so cross your fingers.

00:02:14.579 --> 00:02:19.599
This will be the fourth time in Doctor Who’s
history Coal Hill School is heavily featured.

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:24.069
The first being with Wright and Chesterton,
then with Ace and the Seventh Doctor in Remebrance

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:29.260
of the Daleks, then with the eighth Doctor
and Samatha in The Eight Doctors book story

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.990
and most recently with Jenna Louise Coleman
in the 50th Anniversary Special.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.219
What is his relationship with Clara going
to be?

00:02:35.219 --> 00:02:39.129
Probably not like Rory just because that’s
been done so recently.

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:43.099
When I first saw him I thought of Mickey just
because he had a close relationship with Rose

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:45.319
but it was always implied that he fancied
her.

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:48.510
It didn’t help that Noel Clarke recently
took this picture with Jenna Louise Coleman

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.150
while she was filming Series 8.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:54.170
He said he was just visiting because he was
nearby, but all you conspiracy theorists can

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.230
have fun with it.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.129
I am expecting Series 8 to be less of a relationship
comedy that Matt Smith’s run had become,

00:03:01.129 --> 00:03:03.140
especially with the addition of River Song.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.890
Also rumored to make an appearance.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:09.890
The real question now is which episode Anderson
will debut in if not episode 1, what his arc

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:14.569
is going to be and if there will be any other
new companions.

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:18.590
We have learned quite a bit about episode
1 already, like the fact it takes place in

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:23.189
Victorian London and will feature the Paternoster
Gang and maybe even Jack the Ripper as one

00:03:23.189 --> 00:03:24.189
of the villains.

00:03:24.189 --> 00:03:27.890
I’d say Anderson could be like a history
professor or expert on the subject, but really

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:31.249
isn’t the Doctor supposed to be the universe’s
greatest historian?

00:03:31.249 --> 00:03:33.170
Having lived through most of it himself.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:37.501
Ben Wheatley the director said in a recent
interview this month that he hoped his episodes,

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:40.849
Episodes 1 and 2 will be aired as soon as
July.

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:46.469
Last year the BBC had said Fall 2014 would
be their expected start date, but it’s possible

00:03:46.469 --> 00:03:50.239
that they could air the first episode at San
Diego Comic Con.

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:53.920
Last year they only brought two short clips
for the 50th Anniversary and An Adventure

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.179
in Time and Space.

00:03:55.179 --> 00:03:57.919
But they have screened full epsiodes early
in the past.

00:03:57.919 --> 00:04:03.140
I was able to see the first episode of Series
7 at Wondercon.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.830
The timing was very close to the official
premiere, so it’s possible that we’ll

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:11.260
see new episodes as soon as August if they
do screen it at Comic Con at the end of July.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.590
Now it’s your turn, let me know what your
reactions are to Anderson’s casting and

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:16.310
what kind of a companion you think he’ll
be.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:20.370
I’ll be posting that Q&amp;A video in the next
day or two so be sure to subscribe to get

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.370
it.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:24.570
You can include any questions you want about
series 8.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.670
Right now click here to learn about my top
10 fantasy picks for new Time Lords and click

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.240
here to learn more about series 8.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.430
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.050
High Fives!

